sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If from a medial area a rational area is subtracted, then there arise two other irrational straight lines, either a first apotome of a medial straight line or a straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole.
----
proof:

Let the rational area {BD} be subtracted from the medial area {BC|BCc}.

I say that the side of the remainder {EC} becomes one of two irrational straight lines, either a first apotome of a medial straight line or a straight line which produces with a rational area a medial whole.

